<section class="process spacing">
    <h1>Process</h1>
    <ul id="gallery">
        <li id="process4/1">
            <img src="img/depthsprocess1.png" alt="">
            <p>Since I knew I wanted to use my own old sketches I started by going
                 into my old sketchbooks and pulling out all these drawings. I 
                 decided to use my original character as a constant throughout. </p>
        </li>
        <li id="process4/2">
            <img src="img/depthsprocess2.png" alt="">
            <p>Being a booklet I started structuring with just the text before 
                exploring with the images. I played with the body copy and callout 
                quotes as just other assets to create a story through these compositions. </p>
        </li>
        <li id="process4/3">
            <img src="img/depthsprocess3.png" alt="">
            <p>I originally meant to scan my sketches as cleanly as possible but because 
                I would inconsistently have access to one I started taking pictures 
                with my phone, which led to shadows in my original images. When I would 
                edit the images, trying to get as close to an actually scanned image, 
                I would get images blown out which had a fun effect that I loved. </p>
        </li>
        <li id="process4/4">
            <img src="img/depthsprocess4.png" alt="">
            <p>As I started putting together images and text I tried to let the images 
                speak and be the star of the show. And manipulating sketches to create 
                some stunning spreads. </p>
        </li>
    </ul>
    <ul class="buttons">
        <a href="#process4/1"></a>
    <a href="#process4/2"></a>
    <a href="#process4/3"></a>
    <a href="#process4/4"></a>
    </ul>
</section>